top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135171650.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Starting October 27, Indian Railways will provide travelers the option to include an Optional Travel Insurance Scheme with their reservation ticket purchases. For a nominal fee of just 45 paise, passengers gain crucial coverage for accident-related incidents. The insurance offers various payout options tailored to medical and logistical emergencies. Reservation staff will be responsible for informing ticket buyers about this crucial add-on before finalizing bookings.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/45-paise-for-rs-10-lakh-cover-railways-extends-insurance-to-counter-tickets-from-october-27/articleshow/135171650.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/45-paise-for-rs-10-lakh-cover-railways-extends-insurance-to-counter-tickets-from-october-27/articleshow/135171650.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T19:05:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Arvind Chauhan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135171751,imgsize-233184.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amit Shah visits Delhi police headquarters amid law and order concerns]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-visits-delhi-police-headquarters-amid-law-and-order-concerns/articleshow/135171624.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135171624.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-visits-delhi-police-headquarters-amid-law-and-order-concerns/articleshow/135171624.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-visits-delhi-police-headquarters-amid-law-and-order-concerns/articleshow/135171624.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2